Let $r$ be a Frobenius-semisimple Weil representation on a finite-dimensional complex vector space $V$, with finite inertial image. If $N$ and $N'$ are nilpotent operators such that $(r,N)$ and $(r,N')$ are Weil–Deligne representations, then $$\frac{L(1-s,(r,N)^\vee)}{L(s,(r,N))}
 \doteq
 \frac{L(1-s,(r,N')^\vee)}{L(s,(r,N'))}.$$ More precisely, put $W=V^{r(I_k)}$, $K=\ker(N|_W)$, and $F=r(\mathrm{Fr})$. If $R_N(s)$ denotes the ratio on the left, then $$\label{eq:monodromy-ratio-unit}
 \frac{R_0(s)}{R_N(s)}
   =\det\bigl(-Q^{-s}F\mid W/K\bigr).$$
